off-diagonal (random pair) mean = 0.4531   min = 0.2506   max = 0.7238
gap (diag - off mean)             = +0.4304

Interpretation:
  - If diag - off >> 0:  no-task IS discriminative, and ~0.88 self-match
    means the upstream really did use no-task (or very close). In that
    case, encoding queries with no-task and using the stored vectors
    could work without re-embedding.
  - If diag - off ~ 0:   no-task is non-discriminative; 0.88 is just
    the baseline cosine of any two no-task vectors. Re-embedding (with
    a proper query/passage task pair) remains the right answer.
